# Commits git blame skips. GitHub reads this file by name. Locally, pass
#   git blame --ignore-revs-file .git-blame-ignore-revs <path>
# or set blame.ignoreRevsFile once. Each entry is a FULL 40-character sha: an
# abbreviated one makes git blame fatal, and a sha a rebase has rewritten is
# skipped silently, so an entry is written only after its commit is on origin.
# A blank line changed only in an entry stays on it: blame has no content to match
# it on. `git blame -w` moves those too.

